// Stop treating this as bot detection; treat it as an incentive problem
def route_incoming_request(req):
    // 1. Reward declaration: offer faster/structured data if the agent proves delegation
    if proof := req.headers.get('Agent-Delegation-Token'):
        user_scope = verify_cryptographic_delegation(proof) # extracts user-granted permissions
        strip_brand_ad_pixels(req) # prevent burning viewable CPMs on non-human parsers
        log_synthetic_touchpoint(req.session, user_scope.provenance)
        return serve_agent_contract_api(req, user_scope) # direct JSON, dynamic pricing, clear intent

    // 2. Fallback heuristic: probabilistic entropy (timing jitter, synthetic DOM interaction)
    synthetic_prob = score_behavioral_entropy(req.telemetry, req.headers)

    // 3. Isolate telemetry rather than hard-blocking (blocking just trains better spoofers)
    if synthetic_prob > THRESHOLD:
        quarantine_from_human_analytics_baseline(req.session_id)
        nullify_viewability_and_attribution_credit(req)
        return serve_unoptimized_html(req) # let them scrape, but don't pollute ad metrics

    return serve_standard_human_web(req) # standard TCF/CMP and tracking stack

Don’t train the nets to guess by gait, nor trust what bots confess;
Begin with signed, short-lived intent, and label guesses “guess.”

Let users grant each purpose, scope, and touchpoint they consent;
Have agents, browsers, shops record where every claim was sent.

Pilot with a willing few; seed audits with a labeled stream;
Unknown stays least-privileged—not fraud, nor human in the scheme.

Payment proofs can clear a sale, not prove who saw the glow;
Spoofs and rival interests remain, and still we may not know.
